<title>FRANCE: TABLE - French audit assessment of public deficits. [CORRECTED 17:05 GMT]</title>
<headline>TABLE - French audit assessment of public deficits. [CORRECTED 17:05 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is an assessment of French public deficits according to an audit of public finances made public on Monday. The audit calculated a best case (low) and worst case (high) scenario. Figures in billions of French francs unless otherwise indicated.</p>
<p>				    1997   March    Audit</p>
<p>				  budget*  1997** low  high	gap</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Central Government deficit</p>
<p> national accting standards -285    n/a  -312 -322     -27/-37</p>
<p> EU accounting standards    -277   -275  -303 -313     -28/-38</p>
<p>Social Security		 -24.6 -34.8   -44  -49	-9/-14</p>
<p>Other administration	   15.6  25.7  28.5 26.5     0.8/2.8</p>
<p>France Telecom transfer	37.5  37.5  37.5 37.5</p>
<p>--</p>
<p>Total (EU standards)	 -248.5-246.6  -281 -298 -34.4/-51.4</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>pct of GDP			 3.05  3.03  3.49 3.70  0.46/0.67</p>
<p>(*) Initial 1997 Finance Act voted in September 1997.</p>
<p>(**) French monetary union convergence plan presented to European Union in March 1997.</p>
<p>(Corrects to make format of table more easily readable.)</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
